## 4. Core Web Vitals budget (enforceable rules)

Target: **LCP < 2.5 s, CLS < 0.1, INP < 200 ms** at the 75th percentile, on mobile.

### LCP — Largest Contentful Paint

- The **intent header** on `/sins/[slug]` and `/good-deeds/[slug]` is server-rendered with its data already
  fetched, and the first page of quotes is prefetched + hydrated (`frontend-plan.md` §2.1, TECHNICAL_PLAN E10).
  Never move it behind a client-only fetch, a `useEffect`, or a `'use client'` boundary that waits for data.
- On these screens the LCP element is usually Arabic text, so font loading (CLS section) is part of LCP.
- Any image uses `next/image` with explicit `width`/`height`, or `fill` inside a container with a fixed aspect
  ratio (`relative aspect-video`). Only the single real LCP image is prioritised. In Next 16 the `priority` prop
  is **deprecated**: use `preload`, or `fetchPriority="high"` / `loading="eager"` as the bundled docs
  (`node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/03-api-reference/02-components/image.md`) recommend. Never prioritise
  more than one image per screen.
- Keep client bundles small: `'use client'` as low as possible, and `next/dynamic` for below-the-fold or
  interaction-only UI (e.g. the picker contents, the share sheet).

### CLS — Cumulative Layout Shift

- Every async content area renders a **`Skeleton` matching the real content's geometry** (same height, padding,
  line count, radius) before data arrives, in `loading.tsx` and in client lists. `QuoteCardSkeleton` mirrors
  `QuoteCard` per `variant`. Never a height-0 → content jump; never a centred spinner where a list will appear.
- Fonts load only through `next/font` (`frontend-plan.md` §4.3: Noto Naskh Arabic + Geist placeholders), exposed
  as `--font-arabic` / `--font-ui`. Keep `display: 'swap'` and the automatic metric-matched fallback
  (`adjustFontFallback`, default on for `next/font/google`; set it explicitly for `next/font/local`). Then the
  final fonts can be swapped in without reflowing text. No `<link>` to Google Fonts, no CSS `@import` of fonts.
- Reserve space for anything that appears later: image boxes, badges, the "load more" button. New pages of
  results append **below** the viewport; toasts (`sonner`) overlay and never push content.
- "Another reminder" (shuffle) re-renders the list under a stable heading, with no scroll jump (§7.2).

### INP — Interaction to Next Paint

- Search/filter inputs debounce at **300 ms**. That includes the sin/deed `Command` search (§3.2) before it
  triggers a fetch, a URL/search-param update, or custom (e.g. Arabic-normalised) filtering. Use one shared
  debounce helper/hook; don't hand-roll a timer per component.
- Never run expensive synchronous work (sorting, filtering, grouping a list) directly in a render body. Memoise
  it with `useMemo`, or move non-urgent updates into `startTransition` / `useDeferredValue`.
- Prefer CSS over JS whenever CSS can do it: hover/focus states, show/hide (`hidden md:block`, `group-hover:`,
  `data-[state=…]:`), simple transitions. No `onMouseEnter` state just to change a style.
- Event handlers do the minimum synchronously (update state, start a mutation). Optimistic UI
  (`useToggleFavorite`) gives instant feedback without waiting on the network.

