## 6. Accessibility is a hard requirement

- **Keyboard-operable**: every interactive shared component works with Tab (logical order, no positive
  `tabIndex`), `Enter`/`Space` activation, and `Escape` to close overlays. Use real `<button>`/`<a>` (via the
  `button` primitive or `asChild`), never a clickable `<div>`.
- **Focus-visible** always uses the ring token (`focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring
  focus-visible:ring-offset-2 ring-offset-background`, or the primitive's built-in equivalent). Never
  `outline-none` / `focus:outline-none` without a visible replacement.
- **Contrast** stays WCAG AA (4.5:1 body, 3:1 large text and UI) **with the real Sakina palette** — every
  foreground/background pair in `globals.css` has a computed ratio in `design-language-sakina.md` §4; two
  dark-mode pairs (`destructive`/`grade-mawdu` text, and `intent-iman-branch` text once it's wired up) land at
  ~4.1–4.4:1 — above the 3:1 large-text/UI floor but under the 4.5:1 small-text one, flagged there with the
  mitigation (don't set that exact pairing in `text-xs` body copy). Don't use `text-muted-foreground` on
  `bg-muted` for essential text without checking.
- **Never colour alone**: hadith grade, quote type, selected/pressed state and errors each pair colour with an
  icon and/or text label. `GradeBadge` always shows the grade word (e.g. صحيح), with an `aria-label` such as
  "حديث صحيح". This carries ARCHITECTURE.md's "authenticity is a first-class property" requirement into the UI
  (`frontend-plan.md` §3.2 `badge`, §7.2).
- Overlays: `DialogTitle` + `DialogDescription` always present (`VisuallyHidden` if not shown); focus returns to
  the trigger on close; after a picker selection navigates, focus moves to the page `<h1>` (§7.1).
- Status changes (filter, shuffle, load more) are announced through an `aria-live="polite"` region.
- Decorative icons get `aria-hidden`; icon-only buttons get a translated accessible name.

