## 7. Keeping the system managed over time

- **The one source of visual truth is the token block in `src/app/globals.css`** (between the 🎨 SWAP POINT
  markers, mapped via `@theme inline`). A component must never locally override a token: no
  `style={{ '--primary': … }}`, no per-component CSS variables standing in for a colour, no `:root` rules outside
  `globals.css`. A new semantic need (e.g. a new intent colour) becomes a new token in `globals.css`, with the
  user's approval, never a one-off value.
- **Before adding a shadcn primitive**, check the already-planned list in `frontend-plan.md` §3.2 (and what's
  actually in `src/components/ui/`). If it's planned but missing, add it with the CLI. Deferred ones (`table`,
  `calendar`, `chart`, `carousel`, `pagination`) need a reason tied to the roadmap phase.
- **Recommended later (not built now):** a dev-only `/dev/design-preview` route that renders every shared
  component in every state (loading / empty / error / populated, `ar` + `en`, light + dark). Gate it to
  development via `src/lib/env.ts` so it 404s in production. Use it for visual regression review before and
  after the real palette lands. It's cheaper than Storybook now. Storybook is a legitimate phase-8 upgrade if
  the team wants it. Propose either to the user before building it.
- A palette or font change that forces a component edit means the component was written wrong
  (`frontend-plan.md` §4.4). Fix the component so the swap stays values-only.

